<title>USA: Mid-American Waste files Chapter 11-court.</title>
<headline>Mid-American Waste files Chapter 11-court.</headline>
<dateline>WILMINGTON, Dela. 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mid-American Waste Systems Inc filed for Chapter 11 protection Tuesday in the U.S. Bankruptcy court in Delaware.</p>
<p>In court papers the company, which is based in Canal Winchester, Ohio listed assets of $61.4 million and liabilities of $371.8 million.</p>
<p>Also filing were more than 30 affiliates of Mid-American.</p>
<p>According to court papers, the company is in the business of solid waste landfill management and hauling.  </p>
<p>Among the 20 largest unsecured creditors are Bankers Trust, with $175 million in senior subordinated notes due February 15, 2003; and W.R. Huff with $26.3 million in senior notes.</p>
<p>No other information is available about the filing at this time.</p>
<p>-- ((New York newsdesk 212-859-1611))</p>
